{"entity": "MMGraphRAG", "type": "method", "description": "MMGraphRAG is a multimodal retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) framework that constructs unified knowledge graphs spanning both textual and visual content, employing spectral clustering for multimodal entity analysis. It links scene graphs with textual representations, though this approach has been noted to suffer from structural blindness. As a baseline RAG framework, MMGraphRAG only adds basic image processing while treating tables and equations as plain text, thereby missing crucial structural information.\n\nMMGraphRAG has been evaluated on several benchmarks. On the DocBench dataset, it achieved an overall accuracy of 61.0%, leading in the Academia, Government, and Unanswerable categories. On MMLongBench, it achieved an overall accuracy of 37.7%.\n\nBeyond benchmark performance, MMGraphRAG has been examined in various failure and error cases. In a multi-panel figure interpretation case, it incorrectly identified VAE as having clearer separation. It incorrectly answered 11,503 million DKK for Novo Nordisk's wages and salaries in 2020. It provided a partially incorrect answer regarding the lowest accuracy GCAN configuration for Twitter15. It incorrectly identified the Bert-To-Bert model with an AUPRC of 0.708 as the highest performer for the Evidence Inference dataset. In a multimodal RAG failure case, it produced an incorrect answer about the NER label generation sequence. In a cross-modal noise case, it provided an incorrect answer regarding joint goal accuracy improvements in the Train domain."}
