ar is also the lowest, at approximately 0.6.\n\n**Right Panel: Model Responses**\nThe right panel presents the answers from four different models to the question posed on the left. Each model's response is contained within a dashed box.\n1.  **GPT-4o-mini**: The response states, 'The removal of the dual co-attention mechanism from the GCAN sub-model resulted in the lowest accuracy for Twitter15.'\n2.  **LightRAG**: The response states, 'Removing the source tweet from the GCAN model resulted in the lowest accuracy for Twitter15, as indicated by a significant drop in performance when using the sub-model that excluded both source tweet embeddings and dual co-attention.'\n3.  **MMGraphRAG**: The response states, 'The removal of the source tweet from the GCAN model resulted in the lowest accuracy for Twitter15, as indicated by significant accuracy drops in the ablation analysis in Figure 4.'\n4.  **RAG-Anything (Correct)**: This box is highlighted with a green checkmark. The response states, 'The removal of the source tweet embeddings and dual co-attention, indicated as model configuration \"-S-A,\" resulted in the lowest accuracy for Twitter15.'\n\nThe figure demonstrates that RAG-Anything correctly identifies the '-S-A' configuration as the lowest accuracy performer, while the baseline models (GPT-4o-mini, LightRAG, MMGraphRAG) provide incorrect or partially incorrect answers, misinterpreting the spatial relationships in the chart."}
